**This file is the single source for what words mean in this repo.** It is a decision document —
changing it follows the Change protocol in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

Write for an intelligent reader who does not know this domain or this stack. A definition that only
makes sense to someone already working here has failed.

Three kinds of term belong, and nothing else: **coined vocabulary** this project invented;
**redefined ordinary words** this project gives a narrower or different meaning (the dangerous ones
— define them even when the word looks obvious); and **domain terms of art** an outsider would not
know. A function, class, file, or library name is a code identifier, not a term.

Each entry: the term, a one-sentence plain-English definition, and where it matters, what it is
**not** or what it is confused with. Keep deprecated and retired terms, marked, so the old word is
not silently reintroduced.

A term missing an entry is added in the same change **only if that change defines a decision**. A
change that implements one rephrases in plain English, or stops and flags the term — a new canonical
term surfacing during implementation means the decision that authorized the work was incomplete.
